  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-16T00:43:28.487Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Any chance we can get the VRChive picture upload either removed or overhauled so that photos aren't just instantly uploaded to an account not owned by the player?\nSome reasons behind the request:\n- The uploads do not come with confirmation prior to upload, so if you accidentally clicked the button too bad.\n- The uploads default to an account owned by vrchat, not the player.  So again, if you took a picture by accident you have no way of removing it.\n- VRChive does not respond to removal requests, see above two points why this can be an issue.\n- The VRChat account the uploads default to now contains TOS breaking images, courtesy of VRChat itself.\nThis functionality should either be removed or overhauled in a way that prompts the user to create their own account first or prompts prior to upload.",
